hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1763","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib that he said: O Messenger of Allah, your uncle Abu Talib used to protect you and benefit you. He said: He is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth of the Fire."
"1764","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man prostrates, seven bones prostrate with him: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet."
"1765","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, likewise."
"1766","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hatim meaning Ibn Abi Saghirrah narrated to us, one of the sons of Abdul-Muttalib narrated to me, he said: Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas came to us in one of those seasons, he said: I heard him saying: My father Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father al-Abbas, that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am your uncle; my age is advanced and my term is near, so teach me something by which Allah will benefit me. He said: O Abbas, you are my uncle, and I avail you nothing against Allah, but ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. He said it three times. Then he came to him at the turn of the year and he said to him the like of that."
"1767","Rawh narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri Hatim ibn Abi Saghirrah narrated to us, a man of the offspring of Abdul-Muttalib narrated to me, he said: Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas came to us and the sons of Abdul-Muttalib attended him, and he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abbas narrating from his father Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am your uncle; my age is advanced, and he mentioned its meaning."
"1768","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, have you benefited Abu Talib with anything, for he used to protect you and grow angry for you? He said: Yes, he is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for that he would be in the lowest depth of the Fire."
"1769","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the son of Adam prostrates, seven bones prostrate with him: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet."
"1770","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala informed us, from his uncle Shuayb ibn Khalid, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Batha, and a cloud passed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know what this is? He said: We said: The cloud. He said: And the rain-bearing cloud. We said: And the rain-bearing cloud. He said: And the lofty cloud. He said: We fell silent. He said: Do you know how much is between the heaven and the earth? He said: We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Between them is a journey of five hundred years, and from each heaven to a heaven is a journey of five hundred years, and the thickness of each heaven is a journey of five hundred years. Above the seventh heaven is a sea, between its bottom and its top as between the heaven and the earth. Then above that are eight mountain goats, between their knees and their hooves as between the heaven and the earth. Then above that is the Throne, between its bottom and its top as between the heaven and the earth. And Allah, Blessed and Most High, is above that, and nothing of the deeds of the sons of Adam is hidden from Him."
"1771","Abdullah said: Muhammad ibn as-Sabbah al-Bazzar and Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"1772","Yazid, he is Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Ismail meaning Ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when Quraysh meet one another they meet them with a pleasant face, and when they meet us they meet us with faces we do not recognize. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became severely angry and said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, faith does not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for Allah and for His Messenger."
"1773","Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abdul-Muttalib ibn Rabiah who said: al-Abbas entered upon the Messenger of Allah and said: We go out and see Quraysh talking, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1774","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: I said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What have you availed your uncle, for he used to protect you and grow angry for you? He said: He is in a shallow part, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth of the Fire."
"1775","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, Kathir ibn Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib informed me, from his father al-Abbas who said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Hunayn. He said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with none but me and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abdul-Muttalib. We kept to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and did not part from him, while he was upon a gray mule, and sometimes Mamar said: white, which Farwah ibn Naamah al-Judhami had gifted to him. When the Muslims and the disbelievers met, the Muslims turned fleeing, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began to spur his mule toward the disbelievers. al-Abbas said: And I was holding the bridle of the mule of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, restraining it, while he hastened without pause toward the polytheists, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith was holding the stirrup of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abbas, call: O companions of as-Samurah. He said: And I was a loud-voiced man, so I said at the highest of my voice: Where are the companions of as-Samurah? He said: By Allah, it was as if their turning when they heard my voice was the turning of cattle to their calves. They said: At your service, at your service. The Muslims advanced and they and the disbelievers fought. The Ansar called out saying: O company of the Ansar. Then the callers shortened it to Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, and called: O Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked while upon his mule as if craning upon it toward their fighting, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is when the battle has intensified. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took pebbles and threw them at the faces of the disbelievers, then said: They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kabah; they are defeated, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: I went to look and the fighting was upon its state as I saw. He said: By Allah, it was only that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, threw them with his pebbles, and I continued to see their edge dull and their affair retreating until Allah defeated them. He said: And it is as if I am looking at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, galloping behind them upon his mule."
"1776","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard az-Zuhri once or twice and did not memorize it, from Kathir ibn Abbas who said: Abbas and Abu Sufyan were with him, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He addressed them and said: Now the battle has intensified, and said: Call: O companions of Surah al-Baqarah."
"1777","Jarir ibn Abdul-Hamid Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abdul-Muttalib ibn Rabiah who said: al-Abbas entered upon the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, we go out and see Quraysh talking, and when they see us they fall silent. The Messenger of Allah grew angry and a vein between his eyes swelled, then said: By Allah, faith does not enter the heart of a person until he loves you for Allah and for my kinship."
"1778","Muhammad ibn Idris meaning ash-Shafii narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid meaning Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sad, from Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet and Messenger."
"1779","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet."
"1780","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Amir ibn Sad, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the servant prostrates, seven bones prostrate with him: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet."
"1781","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from az-Zuhri, Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan an-Nasri informed me that Umar called him and mentioned the hadith. He said: While I was with him, his chamberlain Yarfa came and said: Will you see Uthman and Abdur-Rahman and az-Zubayr and Sad asking permission? He said: Yes, so he admitted them. He remained a little, then came and said: Will you see Ali and Abbas asking permission? He said: Yes, so he gave them permission. When they entered, Abbas said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and this, for Ali, and they were disputing regarding the estates which Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from the wealth of Banu an-Nadir. The group said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between them and relieve one of them from the other. Umar said: Wait. I adjure you by Allah, by Whose permission the heaven and the earth stand, do you know that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity, meaning himself? They said: He did say that. Umar turned to Ali and Abbas and said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that? They said: Yes. He said: I shall narrate to you about this matter. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, singled out His Messenger in this fay with something He did not give anyone besides him, and said: And what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from them, you did not spur to the Capable. This was exclusive to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then, by Allah, he did not keep it apart from you nor prefer himself with it over you. He gave it to you and distributed it among you until there remained of it this wealth. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to spend upon his family a year's maintenance from this wealth, then take what remained and place it as Allah's wealth is placed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, acted thus his life. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and Abu Bakr said: I am the guardian of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Bakr took it and acted in it as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, acted in it."
"1782","Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim who said: Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan an-Nasri informed me and mentioned the hadith. He said: While I was sitting with him, his chamberlain Yarfa came to him and said to Umar: Will you see Uthman and Abdur-Rahman and Sad and az-Zubayr asking permission? He said: Yes, admit them. He said: They entered and greeted and sat. He said: Then Yarfa remained a little, then said to Umar: Will you see Ali and Abbas? He said: Yes, so he gave them permission. When they entered him they sat, and Abbas said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. The group, Uthman and his companions, said: Judge between them and relieve one of them from the other. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Wait. I adjure you by Allah, by Whose permission the heaven and the earth stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity, meaning thereby the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, himself? The group said: He did say that. Umar turned to Ali and Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that? They said: He did say that. Umar said: I shall narrate to you about this matter. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, singled out His Messenger in this fay with something He did not give anyone besides him. Allah Most High said: And what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from them, you did not spur, the verse. This verse was exclusive to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then, by Allah, he neither kept it apart nor preferred himself with it over you. He gave it to you and distributed it among you until there remained of it this wealth. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to spend upon his family a year's maintenance from this wealth, then take what remained of it and place it as Allah's wealth is placed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, acted thus his life. I adjure you by Allah, do you know that? They said: Yes. He said to Ali and Abbas: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that? They said: Yes. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and Abu Bakr said: I am the guardian of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, took it and acted in it as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, acted in it. And you at that time, and he turned to Ali and Abbas, claim that Abu Bakr is in it such and such, and Allah knows that he is in it truthful, righteous, rightly guided, following the truth."
"1783","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to supplicate with. He said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being. He said: Then I came to him another time and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to supplicate with. He said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"1784","Abu Said narrated to us, Qays ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi as-Safar narrated to me, from Ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while his wives were with him, and they screened themselves from me except Maymunah. He said: None shall remain in the house who witnessed the ladud except he is given ladud, except that my oath did not include al-Abbas. Then he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aishah said to Hafsah: Tell him that Abu Bakr is a man who, when he stands in your place, weeps. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. He stood and prayed. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found relief and came, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped back and wanted to move back, and he sat beside him, then recited."
"1785","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi as-Safar narrated to us, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his illness: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Abu Bakr went out and magnified Allah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found rest and went out supported between two men. When Abu Bakr saw him he moved back, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured to him: Your place. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat beside Abu Bakr and recited from the place which Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, had reached of the surah."
"1786","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Maysarah, from al-Abbas who said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and he said: Look, do you see any star in the sky? He said: I said: Yes. He said: What do you see? He said: I said: I see ath-Thurayya. He said: Indeed this ummah shall be ruled, to their number from your loins, by two in a tribulation."
"1787","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abi al-Ashath narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Iyas ibn Afif al-Kindi, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I was a merchant man and came for Hajj, and came to al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib to buy from him some merchandise, and he was a merchant man. By Allah, while I was with him at Mina, a man came out of a tent near him and looked at the sun, and when he saw it had declined, meaning he stood to pray. He said: Then a woman came out of that tent from which that man had come out and stood behind him praying. Then a boy nearing puberty came out of that tent and stood with him praying. He said: I said to al-Abbas: Who is this, O Abbas? He said: This is Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdul-Muttalib, my nephew. He said: I said: Who is this woman? He said: This is his wife Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid. He said: I said: Who is this youth? He said: This is Ali ibn Abi Talib, his cousin. He said: I said: What is this that he does? He said: He prays, and he claims he is a prophet, and none has followed him in his affair except his wife and this youth, his cousin, and he claims that the treasures of Kisra and Qaysar shall be opened to him. He said: Afif, and he is the cousin of al-Ashath ibn Qays, used to say, and he embraced Islam after that and his Islam was good: Had Allah granted me Islam that day, I would have been third with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1788","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah who said: al-Abbas said: There reached him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, some of what people say. He said: He ascended the minbar and said: Who am I? They said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdul-Muttalib. Indeed Allah created creation and placed me in the best of His creation, and made them two groups and placed me in the better group, and created the tribes and placed me in the best tribe, and made them houses and placed me in the best of them as a house. I am the best of you as a house and the best of you as a person."
"1789","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib who said: O Messenger of Allah, have you benefited Abu Talib with anything, for he used to protect you and grow angry for you? He said: Yes, he is in a shallow part of the Fire; were it not for that he would be in the lowest depth of the Fire."
"1790","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abbas ibn Abdul-Muttalib, brother of Abdullah, who said: al-Abbas had a spout upon the road of Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar wore his clothes on Friday, and two young birds had been slaughtered for al-Abbas. When he reached the spout, water mixed with the blood of the two young birds was poured and hit Umar, containing the blood of the two young birds. Umar ordered it removed. Then Umar returned and cast off his clothes and wore clothes other than his clothes, then came and led the people in prayer. al-Abbas came to him and said: By Allah, it is the very place where the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed it. Umar said to al-Abbas: I adjure you to climb upon my back until you place it in the place where the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed it. al-Abbas, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, did that."
